<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Regression for a project written by a PRE-proposal-08-M4 build, which is the
  shape of every project that ever had a plugin on a track before M4 landed.
  Reproduced from a real user file (test4_2.qxp) that no build could open.

  The fixture carries both legacy defects at once, deliberately:

   1. <SPluginSlot> with NO id=. Before M4, SPluginSlot::serializeSelfAttributes
      never called SObject::serializeSelfAttributes, which is what emits id=.
      The loader answered any id-less child with "File is corrupt" and aborted
      the WHOLE project — so the build that wrote such a file could not read it
      back either. The slot is now SKIPPED (nothing can reference an object with
      no id, so it costs exactly that one object) and the project loads.

   2. <SPluginChain> whose <SLink objectId=...> names an object the file does
      not contain — in the real file, the id the slot would have had. The
      loader's outer while(true) rescans until the document is empty, so an
      element that can never resolve made it spin forever: ~3M passes/minute,
      a 900 MB log, an unbounded RSS and a hung load. A pass that consumes
      nothing now reports the dangling reference and drops the element.

  The assertions are the point: the REST of the project must survive both
  recoveries intact. Same audio expectations as load_project_render.qxa, which
  loads the identical project without the two legacy defects — so a recovery
  that quietly ate the cut, the track or the wave fails here.

  If this case ever HANGS rather than fails, defect 2 has regressed: that is
  what the CTest timeout is for.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="legacy_project_recovery">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <load-project path="../legacy_idless_slot.qxp"/>

    <render filename="legacy_project_recovery.wav" format="wav" quality="10"/>

    <!-- 0-1 s: cut plays source sec1 (slip offset via the loaded startOffset) -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="legacy_project_recovery.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.15" maxRms="0.21"/>

    <!-- 1-2 s: source sec2 -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="legacy_project_recovery.wav"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.26" maxRms="0.33"/>

    <!-- past the 2 s cut: silence -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="legacy_project_recovery.wav"
                         startFrame="96000" frameCount="48000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.005"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
